  "status": null,
  "background": [
    {
      "text": "The procedure lets the crew manually activate alternate braking without antiskid when the normal braking mode has failed and the automatic switch to alternate braking has also failed. If that fails too, it asks for the parking brake.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCTM",
          "code": "PR-AEP-BRK",
          "page": "P 1/2",
          "pdf": 396
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It results in the loss of nosewheel steering and of the antiskid function.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCTM",
          "code": "PR-AEP-BRK",
          "page": "P 1/2",
          "pdf": 396
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In alternate braking without antiskid, autobrake and antiskid are inoperative. Brake pressure is limited to 1 000 PSI automatically, to limit the risk of wheel locking and tire burst.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCOM",
          "code": "DSC-32-30-10",
          "page": "P 6/8",
          "pdf": 2047
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "technique": [
    {
      "text": "Sequence the switch to alternate braking in three steps. The PF should: 1. Release the brake pedals. 2. Request the PM to set the A/SKID & N/W STRG sw to OFF. 3. Press the brake pedals, only after the PM has set the sw to OFF.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCTM",
          "code": "PR-AEP-BRK",
          "page": "P 1/2",
          "pdf": 396
        },
        {
          "book": "FCTM",
          "code": "PR-AEP-BRK",
          "page": "P 2/2",
          "pdf": 397
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Full reverse may be used to a complete stop if needed. Below 70 kt, when the crew considers that the aircraft can stop on the runway, set idle reverse. Unless required by an emergency, avoid high reverse thrust at low speed, to avoid engine stall and excessive EGT.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCTM",
          "code": "PR-AEP-BRK",
          "page": "P 1/2",
          "pdf": 396
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When reverse is reduced from REV MAX to REV IDLE, be prepared to perceive a change in the felt deceleration.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCTM",
          "code": "PR-AEP-BRK",
          "page": "P 1/2",
          "pdf": 396
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "During a RTO: if normal braking is inoperative, immediately apply the LOSS OF BRAKING memory items.",
      "applies_to": [
        "all"
      ],
      "refs": [
        {
          "book": "FCTM",
          "code": "PR-AEP-MISC",
          "page": "P 21/32",
          "pdf": 466
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
